B08d9 — explicit patched strptime compatibility profile, 2026-09-28
================================================================

The frozen library's parse-only %s and four-digit %z are intentional choices,
not newly discovered EvoCC defects. This user-approved dependency supplement
chooses useful concrete extensions without changing the original benchmark:
  %s: signed epoch seconds -> localtime_r in the current TZ; reject integer,
      time_t and broken-down-calendar overflow; commit tm only after success;
      preserve existing errno on successful parsing; clear an earlier pending
      century/year conversion so it cannot overwrite the resulting full date.
  %z: signed HH or HHMM, 00..23 hours and 00..59 minutes, exact prefix consumption;
      reject incomplete numeric offsets without modifying tm_gmtoff.
Other conversions are unchanged. No blanket glibc/locale/colon-offset claim.

Primary background: musl's 2018 review explicitly warns about signed parsing,
time_t overflow and the TZ choice:
https://www.openwall.com/lists/musl/2018/07/16/1
Its 2025 libc-test discussion confirms the two intentional old limitations:
https://www.openwall.com/lists/musl/2025/08/20/2
We extend the isolated library implementation; we DO NOT take the alternative
of deleting/changing libc-test's two original assertions.

45 checks per small fixture: three fixed-offset zones, pre-epoch and post-2038
values, epoch fields, adjacent century/year ordering, integer/calendar overflow,
truncated/malformed/range-invalid offsets, non-offset fields and suffix pointers.
GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC x O0/O2 x reference/mixed archives:
  Original-library RED: all 36 executions FAIL as expected.
  Patched GREEN: 12 focused runs, 540/540 checks; 24 unchanged original-entry
  replays PASS (strptime and strptime-static share one frozen test object).
  36/36 executions PASS. Both lanes are static; no DSO claim.
  All input hashes and replacement-object link maps verified.
  27 musl adapter tests PASS; Ruff and git diff --check PASS.
After sharing the executor's suite selection, the numerical supplement was
rerun: all 192 executions still PASS (musl-patched-suite-regression-20260928).

Recipe:
  python3 tools/ladder/musl_patched.py --suite time \
    --evocc target/frontend/debug/evocc --output .build/floating-targeted/TIME-NEW
Add --unpatched-control to reproduce original failures. The existing frozen
sources, archives, test objects and benchmark receipt are never overwritten.

